{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>He will rain</b> — He compared the evil that comes upon the wicked suddenly to <i>אַפְעֵי וְחַבְרוֹ</i> [tin-plates and their fellows], which are like the form of burning stones that come down with the rain." "<b>Burning blasts</b> — Like <i>זִלְעָפָה אֲחָזַתְנִי</i> [burning seized me], like trembling." "<b>Their portion</b> — Their lot. Thus <i>ה' מְנַת חֶלְקִי וְכוֹסִי</i> [HaShem is the portion of my lot and my cup], and they are reduplicated stems, and the witness: <i>תִכּוֹסוּ עַל הַשֵּׂה</i>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "The comparison-citation is from Job 21:6 and Psalms 119:53.", 2 "The witness citation 'תכוסו על השה' is textually obscure; its source and meaning are uncertain. I have not identified the reference and translate hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:06.302810774Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}